 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You're building a skyscraper in Mexico City, on an old lake bed. So you set it on footings. Problem solved!",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the soft clay squeezes like toothpaste, and the tower sinks.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pour one giant concrete slab under the whole building, to spread the weight.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the clay is softer on one side, and the whole tower starts to tilt.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you dig a deep basement. The dirt you remove weighs as much as the tower, so it floats.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But the city pumps water from under the clay, and the ground sinks anyway.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you drive piles through the clay, down to a hard layer of sand far below.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The Torre Latinoamericana was built like this, on three hundred sixty one piles.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And it came through the huge earthquakes of 1957 and 1985 still standing.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just built a skyscraper on a lake. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.2
  }
 ],
